    [Doc][Misc] Remove performance profiling setup from GLM examples (#19489)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Remove explicit performance-profiling setup from the GLM-5.2/GLM-5.3 and
    GLM-5.3-Flash deployment examples: six `--profiler-config` arguments,
    their `PROFILE_DIR` variables and directory creation, and the related
    prose. Update the corresponding Chinese translations. Keep
    `profiling_chunk_config` and `--skip-mm-profiling`, which control
    scheduling and multimodal memory estimation, respectively.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. This is a documentation-only update. Example filenames, parameter
    ordering, and serving configurations other than the removed
    performance-profiler setup are preserved.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Markdown lint, spelling checks, and Chinese translation validation
    passed. All six affected shell scripts passed Bash syntax checks;
    comparison of every shell block confirmed that only performance-profiler
    setup was removed. The strict Chinese documentation build passed, and
    generated GLM pages were checked for remaining profiler setup.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
    Signed-off-by: Wyz-134 <298144151+Wyz-134@users.noreply.github.com>
    Co-authored-by: Wyz-134 <298144151+Wyz-134@users.noreply.github.com>

